/-!
# The graded differential forms of the complement of the zero section of a line bundle

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes and `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module. Write `L^⋆ ⟶ X`
for the relative spectrum of the `ℤ`-graded algebra `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}`, the complement of the
zero section of the line bundle. The grading of that algebra grades the pushed-forward de Rham
forms,

`(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S} = ⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}`,

where `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` is generated by the forms `a₀ d a₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d aₚ` with each `aᵢ`
homogeneous and the degrees summing to `n`. This is the sheaf-level version of Tag 0FU9, whose
ring-level statement is `KaehlerDifferential.gradedDifferentialFormComponent`, and it is the
object the residue sequence of Tag 0FUF and the comparisons of Tag 0FUH are statements about.

This file constructs that object: the homogeneous forms over an affine open of `X`, and the
sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaf of the pushforward that they generate.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentToBase`, `Situation.laurentFormsAlgebra` and
  `Situation.laurentForms`: the structure morphism `L^⋆ ⟶ S`, the algebra `Ω^•_{L^⋆/S}` of its
  relative differential forms, and its homogeneous pieces `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFormsPushforward`: **the pushforward
  `(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}`**, an `𝒪_X`-module.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentChartIso` and `Situation.laurentSectionsIso`: **the affine
  local model of `L^⋆`** — over an affine open `U` of `X` the inverse image of `U` in `L^⋆` is
  the spectrum of `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}(U)`, and its ring of functions is that direct sum.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFunction`: **a homogeneous function on `L^⋆`**, the
  function attached to a local section of `L^{⊗ n}` over an affine open of `X`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferential`: the relative de Rham differential of a
  local function on `L^⋆`, as a `1`-form.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm`: **the homogeneous generators**
  `a₀ d a₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d aₚ` of total degree `n`, over an affine open of `X`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.gradedLaurentForms`: **the degree-`n` part
  `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` of the pushed-forward de Rham forms**, as a sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaf of
  `(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFunction_mul` and `Situation.laurentFunction_one`: the
  homogeneous functions are multiplicative in the degree and carry the algebra unit to `1`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentSectionsIso_surjective`: every function on the inverse
  image of an affine open of `X` comes from the Laurent algebra.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.isQuasicoherent_laurentFormsPushforward`: **the pushforward
  `(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` is quasi-coherent**, by Tag 02KG, the projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X` being
  affine.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.exists_affine_trivializing_cover_over_affine`: **`X` is covered
  by affine opens over which `L` is trivial and which map into an affine open of `S`**, the
  cover every local computation in this section is carried out over.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.mem_gradedLaurentForms`: **every homogeneous form of degree `n`
  is a section of `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}`.**
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.gradedLaurentForms_le_iff`: **`Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` is the smallest
  sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaf containing the homogeneous forms of degree `n`**, which is the
  induction principle its consumers use.

## Implementation notes

The homogeneous functions are only available over an *affine* open `U` of `X`: what identifies a
function on the inverse image of `U` with an element of `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}(U)` is the chart of
the relative spectrum, `Stacks.RelativeSpec.GluedSpectrum.chartIsoPreimage`, which exists for
affine `U` only. That is no loss, since the affine opens are a basis of the topology and the
degree-`n` part is defined as the sub-*sheaf* generated by the homogeneous forms: a submodule
sheaf containing them over every affine open contains everything locally built from them.

`Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` is defined as an infimum in the complete lattice
`SheafOfModules.Submodule` of Mathlib rather than as a sectionwise span. A sectionwise span of
the homogeneous forms is not a sheaf — a section of the pushforward is only locally a finite sum
of homogeneous ones, a point the Stacks Project makes by working over affine opens — so taking
the infimum is what makes the construction land in sheaves at all, and it is also exactly the
"generated by" of Tag 0FU9. The price is that the characterization over an affine open is a
theorem rather than a definition, and it is not proved here.

Degrees of forms are carried as integers, the index of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms`, but the recursion defining the
homogeneous generators runs over `ℕ`. The two agree definitionally: `((p + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)` is
`(p : ℤ) + 1` by `rfl`, so wedging a `p`-form with a `1`-form through
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mul (p : ℤ) 1` lands in the `(p + 1)`-forms with no transport
along an equality of degrees, and none of the `HEq` statements that such a transport forces
appear.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FU9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FU9), the grading of the de
  Rham complex of a graded algebra; this file is its sheaf-level counterpart for `L^⋆`
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FUF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FUF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FUH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FUH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01LP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01LP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u v₁ u₁

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-- **Membership in an infimum of sub-sheaves of modules is membership in each of them**, the
infimum of `SheafOfModules.Submodule` being computed sectionwise. -/
theorem mem_sInf_obj {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R} (s : Set M.Submodule)
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M.val.obj X) :
    x ∈ (sInf s).obj X ↔ ∀ N ∈ s, x ∈ N.obj X := by
  rw [_root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSubmodule_sInf,
    PresheafOfModules.Submodule.sInf_obj]
  simp

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace Stacks.LineBundle

variable (D : Situation.{u})

/-! ### The de Rham forms of `L^⋆` over the base and their pushforward -/

/-- The structure morphism `L^⋆ ⟶ S` of the complement of the zero section over the base of the
situation: its projection to `X` followed by `f`. -/
def Situation.laurentToBase : D.laurentSpectrum ⟶ D.S :=
  D.laurentSpectrumToBase ≫ D.f

/-- The algebra `Ω^•_{L^⋆/S}` of relative differential forms of the complement of the zero
section of the line bundle, as a sheaf of graded algebras on `L^⋆`. -/
abbrev Situation.laurentFormsAlgebra :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u}
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf D.laurentSpectrum.toRingedSpace) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.deRhamAlgebras D.laurentToBase).exterior

/-- The sheaf `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` of relative differential `p`-forms of the complement of the zero
section of the line bundle. -/
abbrev Situation.laurentForms (p : ℤ) : D.laurentSpectrum.Modules :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms D.laurentToBase p

/-- The pieces of the algebra of relative differential forms of `L^⋆` are the sheaves of
relative differential forms, so only one notion of form occurs. -/
theorem Situation.laurentFormsAlgebra_piece (p : ℤ) :
    D.laurentFormsAlgebra.piece p = D.laurentForms p :=
  rfl

/-- **The pushforward `(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` of the relative differential `p`-forms of the
complement of the zero section**, an `𝒪_X`-module. The grading of the algebra
`⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}` decomposes it, and `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.gradedLaurentForms` is its
degree-`n` part. -/
def Situation.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} D.X.ringCatSheaf :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj (D.laurentForms p)

/-- The pushforward of the relative differential forms of `L^⋆` is the pushforward of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pushforward`, read at the spelling
`SheafOfModules D.X.ringCatSheaf` of `D.X.Modules`; the two are the same type by definition. -/
theorem Situation.laurentFormsPushforward_eq (p : ℤ) :
    D.laurentFormsPushforward p =
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj (D.laurentForms p) :=
  rfl

/-- The sections of the pushforward of the relative differential forms over an open of `X` are
the forms on its inverse image in `L^⋆`. -/
theorem Situation.laurentFormsPushforward_sections (p : ℤ) (U : D.X.Opens) :
    Γ(D.laurentFormsPushforward p, U) = Γ(D.laurentForms p, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
  rfl

/-- The relative de Rham differential of a local function on `L^⋆`, as a relative `1`-form: the
universal relative derivation followed by the degree-one generator of the exterior algebra. -/
def Situation.laurentDifferential (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens)
    (b : D.laurentSpectrum.sheaf.obj.obj (op V)) : (D.laurentForms 1).val.obj (op V) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase)).val.app (op V)
    (((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation D.laurentToBase).app (op V)).d b)

/-- **The projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X` is an affine morphism**, being the structure morphism of a
relative spectrum. -/
instance Situation.isAffineHom_laurentSpectrumToBase :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom D.laurentSpectrumToBase :=
  Stacks.RelativeSpec.isAffineHom_toBase D.laurentRelativeSpecSituation

/-- **The relative differential `p`-forms of `L^⋆` over `S` are quasi-coherent**, being an
exterior power of the quasi-coherent sheaf of relative differentials. -/
theorem Situation.isQuasicoherent_laurentForms (p : ℕ) :
    (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).IsQuasicoherent :=
  have : (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials
      D.laurentToBase).IsQuasicoherent :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isQuasicoherent_relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase
  Scheme.Modules.isQuasicoherent_exteriorPower
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase) p

/-- **The pushforward `(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module**: the
projection `L^⋆ ⟶ X` is affine and the forms are quasi-coherent, so Tag 02KG applies. The
degree-`n` parts below are sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaves of this. -/
theorem Situation.isQuasicoherent_laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℕ) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward D.laurentSpectrumToBase).obj
      (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ))).IsQuasicoherent :=
  have := D.isQuasicoherent_laurentForms p
  inferInstance

/-! ### The affine local model of `L^⋆` -/

/-- **The affine local model of the complement of the zero section**: over an affine open `U` of
`X` the inverse image of `U` in `L^⋆` is the spectrum of the ring `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}(U)` of
sections of the Laurent algebra sheaf. This is the chart of the relative spectrum of Tag 01LP. -/
def Situation.laurentChartIso (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    Spec (Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.sections D.laurentAlgebraSheaf U.1) ≅
      (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).toScheme :=
  (Stacks.RelativeSpec.gluedSpectrum D.laurentRelativeSpecSituation).chartIsoPreimage U

/-- The global sections of the two sides of the affine local model of `L^⋆`. -/
def Situation.laurentTopIso (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    Γ(Spec (Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.sections D.laurentAlgebraSheaf U.1), ⊤) ≅
      Γ((D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).toScheme, ⊤) where
  hom := (D.laurentChartIso U).inv.appTop
  inv := (D.laurentChartIso U).hom.appTop
  hom_inv_id := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, Iso.hom_inv_id, Scheme.Hom.id_appTop]
  inv_hom_id := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, Iso.inv_hom_id, Scheme.Hom.id_appTop]

/-- **The functions on the inverse image of an affine open `U` of `X` in `L^⋆` are
`⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} L^{⊗ n}(U)`.** This is the local computation identifying
`(L^⋆ → X)_* 𝒪_{L^⋆}` with the Laurent algebra of the line bundle. -/
def Situation.laurentSectionsIso (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.sections D.laurentAlgebraSheaf U.1 ≅
      Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
  (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).symm ≪≫ D.laurentTopIso U ≪≫
    (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).topIso

/-- **A homogeneous function on `L^⋆`**: the function attached, over an affine open `U` of `X`,
to a local section of the `n`th tensor power of the line bundle. -/
def Situation.laurentFunction (n : ℤ) (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    (x : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece n).val.obj (op U.1)) :
    D.laurentSpectrum.sheaf.obj.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) :=
  (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl n U.1 x)

/-- A homogeneous function on `L^⋆` is the image of the homogeneous section of the Laurent
algebra under the comparison of the affine local model. -/
theorem Situation.laurentFunction_eq (n : ℤ) (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    (x : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece n).val.obj (op U.1)) :
    D.laurentFunction n U x =
      (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl n U.1 x) :=
  rfl

/-- **The homogeneous functions on `L^⋆` multiply by adding degrees**: the product of the
functions of two homogeneous local sections is the function of their graded product. -/
theorem Situation.laurentFunction_mul (n m : ℤ) (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    (x : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece n).val.obj (op U.1))
    (y : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece m).val.obj (op U.1)) :
    D.laurentFunction n U x * D.laurentFunction m U y =
      D.laurentFunction (n + m) U ((D.laurentAlgebra.mul n m).app (op U.1) x y) :=
  (map_mul (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl n U.1 x)
      (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl m U.1 y)).symm.trans
    (congrArg (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl_mul n m U.1 x y))

/-- **The unit of the Laurent algebra is the constant function `1` on `L^⋆`.** -/
theorem Situation.laurentFunction_one (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    D.laurentFunction 0 U (D.laurentAlgebra.one.eval (op U.1)) = 1 :=
  (congrArg (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom (D.laurentAlgebraSheafIncl_one U.1)).trans
    (map_one (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom)

/-- **Every function on the inverse image of an affine open of `X` in `L^⋆` comes from the
Laurent algebra**, the comparison of the affine local model being an isomorphism. -/
theorem Situation.laurentSectionsIso_surjective (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    Function.Surjective (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom.hom :=
  fun b => ⟨(D.laurentSectionsIso U).inv.hom b, by
    change ((D.laurentSectionsIso U).inv ≫ (D.laurentSectionsIso U).hom).hom b = b
    rw [Iso.inv_hom_id]
    rfl⟩

/-! ### The homogeneous forms and the graded pieces -/

/-- **The homogeneous relative differential forms of degree `n` on `L^⋆`**, over an affine open
`U` of `X`: the forms `a₀ d a₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d aₚ` whose coefficients `aᵢ` are homogeneous functions of
degrees summing to `n`. The recursion wedges one `d aᵢ` on at a time, on the right. -/
def Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm (D : Situation.{u}) (U : D.X.affineOpens) :
    (p : ℕ) → ℤ →
      (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).val.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) → Prop
  | 0, n, ω => ∃ x : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece n).val.obj (op U.1),
      ω = D.laurentFunction n U x •
        D.laurentFormsAlgebra.one.eval (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
  | (p + 1), n, ω => ∃ (i j : ℤ) (_ : i + j = n)
      (η : (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).val.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      (x : (D.laurentAlgebra.piece j).val.obj (op U.1)),
      Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm D U p i η ∧
        ω = (D.laurentFormsAlgebra.mul (p : ℤ) 1).app
              (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) η
            (D.laurentDifferential _ (D.laurentFunction j U x))

/-- **The degree-`n` part `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` of the pushed-forward relative differential forms of
the complement of the zero section of a line bundle**: the smallest sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaf of
`(L^⋆ → X)_* Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` containing, over every affine open of `X`, the homogeneous forms of
degree `n`. This is the sheaf-level counterpart of the graded components of Tag 0FU9. -/
@[stacks 0FU9 "the sheaf-level graded components of the pushed-forward de Rham forms of L-star"]
def Situation.gradedLaurentForms (p : ℕ) (n : ℤ) :
    (D.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ)).Submodule :=
  sInf {N : (D.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ)).Submodule |
    ∀ (U : D.X.affineOpens)
      (ω : (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).val.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))),
      Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm D U p n ω → ω ∈ N.obj (op U.1)}

/-- **Every homogeneous form of degree `n` is a section of `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}`** over its affine
open. -/
theorem Situation.mem_gradedLaurentForms {p : ℕ} {n : ℤ} (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    {ω : (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).val.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))}
    (hω : Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm D U p n ω) :
    ω ∈ (D.gradedLaurentForms p n).obj (op U.1) := by
  rw [Situation.gradedLaurentForms]
  refine (Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sInf_obj
    (M := D.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ)) _ (op U.1) ω).mpr ?_
  exact fun _ hN => hN U ω hω

/-- **`Ω^p_{L^⋆/S, n}` is the smallest sub-`𝒪_X`-module sheaf of the pushforward containing the
homogeneous forms of degree `n`**: this is the induction principle for proving that a property
closed under the sheaf and module operations holds for all sections of the degree-`n` part. -/
theorem Situation.gradedLaurentForms_le_iff {p : ℕ} {n : ℤ}
    (N : (D.laurentFormsPushforward (p : ℤ)).Submodule) :
    D.gradedLaurentForms p n ≤ N ↔
      ∀ (U : D.X.affineOpens)
        (ω : (D.laurentForms (p : ℤ)).val.obj (op (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))),
        Situation.IsHomogeneousLaurentForm D U p n ω → ω ∈ N.obj (op U.1) :=
  ⟨fun h U _ hω => h (op U.1) (D.mem_gradedLaurentForms U hω), fun h => sInf_le h⟩

/-! ### A trivializing affine cover adapted to the base -/

/-- **Every point of `X` has an affine open neighbourhood over which the line bundle is
trivial and which maps into an affine open of `S`.** This is the cover the local computation of
the graded forms is carried out over: trivializing the line bundle makes the inverse image in
`L^⋆` the spectrum of a Laurent polynomial algebra, and mapping into an affine open of `S` makes
the relative differentials of that spectrum the Kähler differentials of a ring map. -/
theorem Situation.exists_trivializing_affineOpen_over_affine (x : D.X) :
    ∃ (U : D.X.affineOpens) (V : D.S.affineOpens), x ∈ U.1 ∧ U.1 ≤ D.f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ∧
      Nonempty (D.L.over U.1 ≅ SheafOfModules.unit (D.X.ringCatSheaf.over U.1)) := by
  obtain ⟨I, W, hW, e⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.IsLocallyTrivial.exists_trivializing_cover (M := D.L)
  obtain ⟨i, hxi⟩ := ((Opens.coversTop_iff (↥D.X) W).mp hW).exists_mem x
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, -⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp D.S.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show D.f.base x ∈ (⊤ : D.S.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, hUle⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp D.X.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show x ∈ W i ⊓ D.f ⁻¹ᵁ V from ⟨hxi, hxV⟩)
  exact ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, ⟨V, hV⟩, hxU, hUle.trans inf_le_right,
    ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.isoUnitOverOfHom D.L
      (homOfLE (hUle.trans inf_le_left)) (e i).some⟩⟩

/-- **The affine opens over which the line bundle is trivial and which map into an affine open of
`S` cover `X`.** This is the cover of Tag 01CS refined in both of the ways the local computation
of the graded differential forms of `L^⋆` needs. -/
theorem Situation.exists_affine_trivializing_cover_over_affine :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (U : I → D.X.affineOpens) (V : I → D.S.affineOpens),
      (⨆ i, (U i).1) = ⊤ ∧ (∀ i, (U i).1 ≤ D.f ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1) ∧
        ∀ i, Nonempty (D.L.over (U i).1 ≅
          SheafOfModules.unit (D.X.ringCatSheaf.over (U i).1)) := by
  refine ⟨{p : D.X.affineOpens × D.S.affineOpens //
      p.1.1 ≤ D.f ⁻¹ᵁ p.2.1 ∧
        Nonempty (D.L.over p.1.1 ≅ SheafOfModules.unit (D.X.ringCatSheaf.over p.1.1))},
    fun p => p.1.1, fun p => p.1.2, eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ => ?_,
    fun p => p.2.1, fun p => p.2.2⟩
  obtain ⟨U, V, hxU, hUV, hL⟩ := D.exists_trivializing_affineOpen_over_affine x
  exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨(U, V), hUV, hL⟩, hxU⟩

end Stacks.LineBundle

end
